{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## PHASE 1 EXIT — root cause re-confirmed at runtime (rebar-debug)\n\nRe-verified on this machine (scc 3.7.0) rather than re-derived:\n\n    scc --format json src/rebar\n      -> 9 language groups, every \"Files\" is [] (Python 0, JSON 0, Markdown 0, Plain Text 0,\n         YAML 0, HTML 0, JavaScript 0, CSS 0, JSX 0)\n    scc --by-file --format json src/rebar\n      -> 729 file entries, max Code 7011 (src/rebar/_engine/resources/ticket-wordlist-v2.txt)\n\nMechanism, terminating at a changeable artifact: `src/rebar/metrics/analyzers/scc_loc.py`\nbuilds `[\"scc\", \"--format\", \"json\", str(scan_root)]`. Without `--by-file` scc emits per-language\nSUMMARIES whose `Files` key is present-but-empty, so `_parse_files` passes every type check\n(`isinstance(entries, list)` is True) and iterates zero entries. `analyze` then returns\n`AnalyzerResult(loc={\"files\": {}, \"max_loc\": 0})` — a value, not an `Unavailable`.\n\nBEFORE (this worktree, `rebar metrics --output json`):\n\n    module_size_distribution :: {\"count\": 0, \"near_cap_count\": null, \"over_cap_count\": null,\n                                 \"max_loc\": 0}   confidence=high source=structural\n    oversized_module_count   :: null\n    complexity_summary       :: {\"functions\": 18842, \"total_ccn\": 46980, \"max_ccn\": 65,\n                                 files: 1707}    confidence=high source=structural\n    duplication_summary      :: {\"clones\": 1535, \"percentage\": 4.2833}\n\nLegitimacy = `defect`, not intended behaviour. `rebar.metrics.registry.Unavailable` exists\nprecisely to express \"measured nothing\"; returning a zero-valued `AnalyzerResult` for an empty\nmeasurement violates that contract, and epic 839b-f6d2-7e1a-4051's motivating finding was that\nfabricated authoritative zeros are the failure being eliminated. AC2 is the load-bearing item.\n\n## AC3 — the narrowing does NOT belong in `scan_roots`\n\nChecked, per the operator's instruction to consider `scan_roots` first. `scan_roots` is a\nDIRECTORY axis: `_scan_roots` resolves each entry to a `Path` and passes it as scc's positional\nargument. The files that must be excluded are INTERLEAVED inside the directory that must be\nkept — `src/rebar/_engine/resources/*.txt`, `src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor_assets/dist/*.js`,\n`.../src/*.jsx` all live under `src/rebar`. No directory-set can express \"only Python files\nunder src/rebar\", so narrowing by `scan_roots` alone cannot satisfy AC3. The missing axis is\nfile TYPE, which is orthogonal to the directory axis and needs its own expression.\n\n## AC4 — the metric can match the CI gate EXACTLY, not just approximately\n\nThe CI module-size gate measures `find src/rebar -name '*.py' | xargs wc -l` against\n`.github/module-size-limit.txt` (800). The adapter currently reads scc's `Code` field, which\nexcludes blanks and comments and therefore can never equal `wc -l`. scc's per-file entry also\ncarries `Lines`, which is the raw line count. Measured over all 435 Python files under\nsrc/rebar: `Lines` vs `wc -l` mismatches = 0 of 435; max Lines = 800\n(src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py) = exactly the CI cap; max Code = 768. So reading `Lines`\nreconciles the metric with the gate by construction rather than leaving a documented gap.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. AC1 — add `--by-file` to the scc argv.\n2. AC2 — an empty aggregated file map returns `Unavailable`, never a zero-valued\n   `AnalyzerResult`. A zero must mean \"measured zero\", not \"measured nothing\".\n3. AC3 — add `code_health.include_extensions` (`list[str]`, default `[]` = polyglot, unchanged\n   behaviour for every other client), read LIVE in `scc_loc.analyze` where it becomes scc's\n   `--include-ext` argument, threaded through `_commands/metrics.py` -> ctx ->\n   `git_metrics._scc_analysis` (and folded into that function's cache key). Dogfooded in the\n   same change via this repo's `rebar.toml` `[code_health]` table. The adapter stays polyglot;\n   only rebar's own configuration is Python-specific. No inert knob (cf. dce2, idea 94bc).\n4. AC4 — read scc's `Lines` rather than `Code` so `module_size_distribution` measures what the\n   gate enforces; set `size_cap = 800` in `rebar.toml` so near/over-cap counts stop being null.\n5. AC5 — regression test: a scan root that demonstrably contains files must never produce a\n   zero-valued result."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785911595996805001,"uuid":"4a6978cf-405a-452f-86e6-620dafe7dbc1"}